==English==
[[Image:Angeln_zubehoer_grundblei_01.jpg|thumb|right|200px|fishing sinkers]]

===Etymology===
{{affix|en|sink|-er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪŋkə(ɹ)/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-sinker.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋkə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[sink]]s something.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1999|author=David Frank|title=J.B. McLachlan: A Biography
|passage=McLachlan's value as a coal miner was enhanced by the specialized skill he learned as a shaft-'''sinker'''.}}
# {{lb|en|fishing}} A [[weight]] used in [[fishing]] to cause the [[line]] or [[net]] to [[sink]].
#: {{ux|en|Hook the '''sinker''' onto this loop.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1897|author=Rudyard Kipling|title=Captains Courageous
|passage=Then the caplin moved off, and five minutes later there was no sound except the splash of the '''sinkers''' overside, the flapping of the cod, and the whack of the muckles as the men stunned them.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} Any of several high speed pitches that have a downward motion near the plate; a [[two-seam fastball]], a [[split-finger fastball]], or a [[forkball]].
#: {{ux|en|His '''sinkers''' drew one ground ball after another.}}
# {{lb|en|construction}} A [[sinker nail]], used for [[framing]] in current [[construction]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[doughnut]]; a [[biscuit]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1926|author=Edna Ferber|title=Show Boat: A Novel|page=268
|passage=Of the fifty cents, ten went for the glassy shoeshine; twenty-five for a boutonniere; ten for coffee and '''sinkers''' at the Cockeyed Bakery.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=Gerald J. Prokopowicz|title=All for the Regiment: The Army of the Ohio, 1861-1862|page=148
|passage=they improvised by opening a barrel of flour and letting each man dump in a quart of water (if he had one) and scoop out a handful of dough to bake into rock-hard '''sinkers'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=William W. Johnstone|title=Ambush Of The Mountain Man|page=168
|passage="Gonna have to dip them '''sinkers''' in coffee to get 'em soft enough to chew," Jason Biggs said, grinning.}}
# In knitting machines, one of the thin plates, blades, or other devices, that depress the loops upon or between the needles.

